From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sahil Faizal <sahil.faizal@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:45:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] rpp: Keep JPEG padding within each LDS lane slice

For an extra eight-pixel group in a sixteen-aligned tile, validPixels is
negative. Starting the padding loop at that negative value writes the
preceding lane's LDS slice and races with its valid pixel stores.

Start padding at max(validPixels, 0) and fill only the current eight-pixel
slice. Preserve the global lastValidIdx calculation so edge pixels are
replicated correctly even when the whole slice is padding. Apply this to
both packed-source layout variants. CPU checks passed all widths 1..255;
the old loops overlapped 448 LDS slots and the candidate owns each once.

Found by ConcurrencySanitizer in the comprehensive RPP suites:
https://github.com/ROCm/TheRock/actions/runs/43022969021
Source: ROCm/rocm-libraries 2d3b6e98e4ef99cf7dccf54068f333c32a441348
Carry temporarily in TheRock pending upstream RPP review.

Validated in the pinned native build image with source-derived CPU
ownership/value fixtures and a full CSAN gfx942 RPP component build,
staging, and all five RPP artifact components. GPU execution is separate.
---

diff --git a/projects/rpp/src/modules/tensor/hip/kernel/jpeg_compression_distortion.cpp b/projects/rpp/src/modules/tensor/hip/kernel/jpeg_compression_distortion.cpp
index f148fdf..3f030fa 100644
--- a/projects/rpp/src/modules/tensor/hip/kernel/jpeg_compression_distortion.cpp
+++ b/projects/rpp/src/modules/tensor/hip/kernel/jpeg_compression_distortion.cpp
@@ -507,7 +507,7 @@ __global__ void jpeg_compression_distortion_pkd3_hip_tensor(T* srcPtr, uint2 src
         }
 
         int lastValidIdx = srcIdx + ((validPixels - 1) * 3);
-        for (int i = validPixels; i < min(validPixels + 16, 8); i++) {
+        for (int i = max(validPixels, 0); i < 8; i++) {
             src_smem[hipThreadIdx_y_channel.x][hipThreadIdx_x8 + i] = srcPtr[lastValidIdx];
             src_smem[hipThreadIdx_y_channel.y][hipThreadIdx_x8 + i] = srcPtr[lastValidIdx + 1];
             src_smem[hipThreadIdx_y_channel.z][hipThreadIdx_x8 + i] = srcPtr[lastValidIdx + 2];
@@ -715,7 +715,7 @@ __global__ void jpeg_compression_distortion_pkd3_pln3_hip_tensor(T* srcPtr, uint
         }
         // Pad 16 pixels by duplicating the last valid pixel
         int lastValidIdx = srcIdx + ((validPixels - 1) * 3);
-        for (int i = validPixels; i < min(validPixels + 16, 8); i++) {
+        for (int i = max(validPixels, 0); i < 8; i++) {
             src_smem[hipThreadIdx_y_channel.x][hipThreadIdx_x8 + i] = srcPtr[lastValidIdx];
             src_smem[hipThreadIdx_y_channel.y][hipThreadIdx_x8 + i] = srcPtr[lastValidIdx + 1];
             src_smem[hipThreadIdx_y_channel.z][hipThreadIdx_x8 + i] = srcPtr[lastValidIdx + 2];
